BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:francoise-cite-internationale-arts-clinique-2027@artificialnouveau.gith
 ub.io
DTSTAMP:20260916T111243Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260816
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260817
SUMMARY:Deadline: Association Francoise pour l'oeuvre contemporaine x Cite 
 internationale des arts: Research and Creation Residency 2027
DESCRIPTION:Launched in 2025\, this research and creation residency explore
 s the links between contemporary art\, psychiatry and the human sciences. 
 It is expressly not a therapeutic programme. It seeks artists whose practi
 ce resonates with the notion of the clinical\, meaning a situated approach
  that works closely with lived narratives and specific contexts\, and that
  engages with questions of care. The selected artist receives tailored sup
 port from Albertine de Galbert\, a clinical psychologist and exhibition cu
 rator\, including four to six working sessions\, alongside networking and 
 meeting time with programme partners. Outputs include an ongoing online jo
 urnal\, a mid-residency open studio\, and a closing presentation (exhibiti
 on\, public talk or publication) defined with the artist. Applications go 
 by email as a single PDF of no more than 15 MB to residence@francoiseartme
 mo.fr\, and require a two-page CV\, a ten-page portfolio\, a two-page stat
 ement of intent\, and a letter of recommendation from an institution or a 
 curator. A jury of four to six art and psychiatry specialists decides\, wi
 th results announced in September 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Association Franc
 oise pour l'oeuvre contemporaine / Cite internationale des arts\nLocation:
  Paris\, France (Marais site of the Cite internationale des arts). Open to
  artist-authors of any nationality and any discipline\, mid-career or esta
 blished\, with no age limit. Applicants must be comfortable working in Fre
 nch or English. Note: the studio-apartments do not meet current accessibil
 ity standards for people with disabilities.\nAward: Grant of EUR 1\,000 ne
 t of tax per month\, plus a furnished studio-apartment (20 to 35 sq m\, co
 mbining living and working space)\, international return travel to Paris a
 irports or stations\, travel insurance\, and capped research support again
 st receipts. Additional fees apply for accompanying persons. No applicatio
 n fee.\nDuration: Approximately 12 weeks\, 5 January to 26 March 2027\n\nM
 ore: https://www.citeinternationaledesarts.fr/appels-a-candidature/associa
 tion-francoise-pour-loeuvre-contemporaine-x-cite-internationale-des-arts/?
 utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.citeinternationaledesarts.fr/appels-a-candidature/associati
 on-francoise-pour-loeuvre-contemporaine-x-cite-internationale-des-arts/?ut
 m_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Paris\, France (Marais site of the Cite internationale des arts). 
 Open to artist-authors of any nationality and any discipline\, mid-career 
 or established\, with no age limit. Applicants must be comfortable working
  in French or English. Note: the studio-apartments do not meet current acc
 essibility standards for people with disabilities.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:bloedel-reserve-creative-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260916T111243Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: Creative Residency at Bloedel Reserve: Class of 2027
DESCRIPTION:Bloedel Reserve's residency programme exists to foster creative
  thinking inspired by nature and to explore the connection between humans 
 and the environment. It is open to professional and emerging artists\, com
 posers\, writers\, botanists\, landscape architects\, researchers and othe
 rs working on themes of nature and human connection to it. Residents get a
  three-week stay at a 140-acre internationally recognised public garden an
 d forest preserve\, housed in a small home hidden in the woods off the mai
 n paths. Note for non-US applicants: the funding is structured as expense 
 reimbursement rather than a stipend\, capped at USD 1\,000\, which for tra
 nsatlantic applicants is unlikely to cover airfare plus meals over three w
 eeks.\n\nOrganisation: Bloedel Reserve\nLocation: Bainbridge Island\, Wash
 ington\, USA\, between Seattle and the Kitsap Peninsula\, reachable by fer
 ry from Seattle or by car via the Kitsap Peninsula. Residents must be 21 o
 r older. International applicants are eligible but are funded differently 
 from domestic ones (see amount).\nAward: USD 22 application fee. Furnished
  private house on the grounds with linens\, stocked kitchen\, wi-fi\, laun
 dry and use of a smart car\; an electric piano is available. Domestic resi
 dents receive a USD 1\,000 stipend. International residents receive no sti
 pend and may instead submit up to USD 1\,000 of expenses for reimbursement
 . Residents pay for their own meals and their own travel to Bainbridge Isl
 and. There is no dedicated studio\; residents work in the house.\nDuration
 : Three weeks\; residents stay one at a time with no overlap\n\nMore: http
 s://bloedelreserve.slideroom.com/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&ut
 m_medium=referral#/login/program/88209
URL:https://bloedelreserve.slideroom.com/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrant
 desk&utm_medium=referral#/login/program/88209
LOCATION:Bainbridge Island\, Washington\, USA\, between Seattle and the Kit
 sap Peninsula\, reachable by ferry from Seattle or by car via the Kitsap P
 eninsula. Residents must be 21 or older. International applicants are elig
 ible but are funded differently from domestic ones (see amount).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:archipel-butor-livre-de-dialogue-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260916T111243Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260830
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260831
SUMMARY:Deadline: Archipel Butor Livre de dialogue Creation Residency 2027
DESCRIPTION:Archipel Butor runs its creation residency out of the former ho
 me of the writer Michel Butor in Lucinges\, Haute-Savoie\, and this call i
 s for a livre de dialogue\, a dialogue book made jointly by a writer and a
  visual artist. The residency exists to give a pair concentrated time to d
 evelop a book together and to raise the profile of artist book culture and
  of collaboration at the centre of artistic process. WHO APPLIES: a pair m
 ade up of an author with a project for a dialogue book and a visual artist
  collaborating on it. The two do not need to have worked together before\,
  but both must be present during the shared periods. WHAT IS PROVIDED: EUR
  2\,000 gross per month per artist\, up to two return trips per person wit
 hin France and Europe\, and accommodation in the writer's house. STRUCTURE
 : two months in total\, taken as eight weeks which may be split across the
  year from January 2027\, with 70 percent of the time given to creation an
 d 30 percent to mediation and public engagement activities. A videoconfere
 nce is held with the selected laureates beforehand to arrange on-site sche
 duling and the mediation sessions. HOW TO APPLY: follow the official call 
 document downloadable from the residency page\, submitting a single PDF to
  accueil@archipel-butor.fr containing a joint letter\, biographies of both
  practitioners\, the artistic proposal\, technical specifications and the 
 proposed mediation activities. NOTE: the call and application file are in 
 French. Deadline 30 August 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Archipel Butor\nLocation
 : Lucinges (74380)\, Haute-Savoie\, France\, in the house of the writer Mi
 chel Butor.\nAward: Creation grant of EUR 2\,000 gross per month per artis
 t\, so roughly EUR 4\,000 each across the two months and EUR 8\,000 for th
 e pair. Up to two return journeys per person are covered within France and
  Europe. Accommodation is provided in Michel Butor's writer's house. No ap
 plication fee.\nDuration: Two months in total\, taken as eight weeks that 
 may be split\, starting from January 2027. Time is split 70 percent creati
 on and 30 percent mediation activities.\n\nMore: https://www.archipel-buto
 r.fr/residence-creation/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=
 referral
URL:https://www.archipel-butor.fr/residence-creation/?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Lucinges (74380)\, Haute-Savoie\, France\, in the house of the wri
 ter Michel Butor.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:le-garage-moderne-oasis-residencies-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260916T111243Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: Le Garage Moderne: OASIS International Artist Residencies
  2026 (Bordeaux)
DESCRIPTION:Second year of Le Garage Moderne's residency cycle within the E
 uropean OASIS project\, offering five grants to international artists for 
 two-week stays in Bordeaux. THE SITE IS THE POINT. Le Garage Moderne is a 
 working non-profit car and bicycle workshop with a neighbourhood canteen a
 nd a versatile venue for performing arts\, concerts and community gatherin
 gs\, all at once a productive space\, a public space and a community-drive
 n common. Having just moved back into its 19th-century building after a lo
 ng renovation\, the team describes machines and workbenches back in place 
 and a brand-new playground\, and invites residents to take over the space 
 and explore its physical and social possibilities. They ask for SITE-SPECI
 FIC PROPOSALS that play with the verticality\, the scale of the space\, th
 e community and what they call the hive-like vibe of the venue\, where eve
 ryone runs around\, shouts\, gets their hands dirty and learns in the proc
 ess. DISCIPLINES: any\, explicitly including design\, visual art\, perform
 ing arts\, film\, small-scale architecture\, emergency architecture\, craf
 t-making\, street furniture\, sound\, and interdisciplinary or community-b
 ased practices. Proposals combining artistic creation with the spatial and
  the social are especially encouraged\, and the organisers say plainly tha
 t they want to be surprised. WHAT IS EXPECTED: openness to exchange and co
 llaboration with the 11 permanent residents and with 3 local artists recru
 ited through a separate OASIS call\; participation in 2 days of masterclas
 s open to members and community\, where you describe and share your practi
 ce\, technique and working context with fellow OASIS residents\, local art
 ists\, members and staff\; and a public outcome\, which need not be a larg
 e event but must be something the public can experience. RIGHTS: work prod
 uced during the residency remains the artist's property\, but documentatio
 n of it is made by Le Garage Moderne and will be publicised by them for th
 ree years after the residency. Note this is a different OASIS partner call
  from the OASis In the Park (Naples) and Disappearing Landscape (High Tatr
 as) rounds under the same European project.\n\nOrganisation: Le Garage Mod
 erne (European OASIS project)\nLocation: Bacalan district\, Bordeaux\, Fra
 nce. Le Garage Moderne is a non-profit car garage and bicycle workshop\, a
  canteen serving sponsored meals\, and a cultural venue housing 11 permane
 nt artists\, makers and craftswomen\, recently returned to its 19th-centur
 y building after a two-and-a-half-year renovation.\nAward: Five grants. Ea
 ch artist receives a fee of EUR 1\,300 gross (taxes may apply depending on
  legal status)\, up to EUR 600 for production expenses such as raw materia
 ls\, technical services or special tools\, a lump-sum travel grant scaled 
 to distance with top-ups for green travel options\, a per diem of EUR 45 p
 er day\, and accommodation in a self-catering hotel. Access to the shared 
 tools and spaces of Le Garage Moderne is included\, subject to the associa
 tion's regulations. No application fee.\nDuration: Two weeks on site. Five
  overlapping two-week slots\, and applicants may choose one or more: 9 to 
 22 November\, 16 to 29 November\, 23 November to 6 December\, 30 November 
 to 13 December\, and 7 to 20 December 2026. Deadline 1 September 2026\; pr
 e-selection interviews 15 September\; final selection announced 1 October 
 2026.\n\nMore: https://legaragemoderne.org/oasis2026?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://legaragemoderne.org/oasis2026?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrant
 desk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Bacalan district\, Bordeaux\, France. Le Garage Moderne is a non-p
 rofit car garage and bicycle workshop\, a canteen serving sponsored meals\
 , and a cultural venue housing 11 permanent artists\, makers and craftswom
 en\, recently returned to its 19th-century building after a two-and-a-half
 -year renovation.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:futures-of-listening-earth-immersion-trembling-planet-2027@artificialno
 uveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260916T111243Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260913
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260914
SUMMARY:Deadline: Futures of Listening x KNMI: Earth Immersion\, Trembling 
 Planet Residency
DESCRIPTION:One residency for an artist\, designer or maker working with so
 und\, exploring spatial sound in relation to seismology\, climate and disc
 harge-related acoustics\, run with the Royal Netherlands Meteorological In
 stitute. THE PREMISE: climate change is making major landslides\, ice-brea
 koff events from marine-terminating glaciers\, and sound-producing ice mov
 ements more common. These generate infrasonic vibrations inaudible to huma
 ns that sometimes spread across the entire planet and into the atmosphere.
  The residency asks how immersive sound techniques can make these events t
 angible and build meaningful sonic narratives from them. WHAT YOU GET ACCE
 SS TO: scientific data on seismological events\, vibrations\, infrasound a
 nd the movement of land and ice masses\, with scientific expertise from KN
 MI (lead researcher Jelle Assink) and artistic guidance from the Futures o
 f Listening team\, relating local events to global impact. RESEARCH QUESTI
 ONS to position your proposal against include how immersive sound can cult
 ivate situated listening to ecological processes and more-than-human encou
 nters\, how artistic and scientific methods of working with environmental 
 data can inform each other\, and what is gained\, lost or ethically at sta
 ke when environmental sounds are translated\, interpreted or reconstructed
  through spatial and synthetic means. DELIVERABLE: residents are expected 
 to create a final spatial sound production using the 4DSOUND system. Other
  outcomes may include immersive installations\, data-driven sonic works\, 
 audiovisual pieces\, software prototypes or reusable methodologies. Experi
 ence in art-science environments is welcome but not required\; you may ins
 tead explain why working in one would benefit your practice. HARD ELIGIBIL
 ITY GATE: applicants must be based in the Netherlands AND registered as an
  artist with the Dutch Chamber of Commerce (KvK). This is not negotiable a
 nd rules out non-NL applicants. Futures of Listening is a Netherlands-base
 d platform for spatial sound\, immersive experience\, performance and inst
 allation art\, founded by FIBER Festival\, 4DSOUND\, Robin Koek and Art of
  Sound at the Royal Conservatoire The Hague\, supported by CIIIC and Stimu
 leringsfonds.\n\nOrganisation: Futures of Listening (FIBER\, 4DSOUND\, Rob
 in Koek\, Art of Sound) in collaboration with KNMI\, the Royal Netherlands
  Meteorological Institute\nLocation: Partially self-hosted\, partially at 
 the 4DSOUND studio in Amsterdam\, and partially at KNMI in De Bilt near Ut
 recht\, Netherlands.\nAward: Total residency fee of EUR 7\,125\, calculate
 d as 25 commissioned days at a day rate of EUR 285. Six of those 25 days c
 an be spent at the 4DSOUND studio working with their team. Some additional
  financial support is available if needed\, including material and travel 
 costs\, but these must be clearly defined and agreed before the residency 
 starts. No application fee.\nDuration: January to March 2027\, structured 
 as 25 commissioned days. Deadline 13 September 2026.\n\nMore: https://fibe
 r.homerun.co/artist-residency-earth-immersion/en?utm_source=artificialnouv
 eaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://fiber.homerun.co/artist-residency-earth-immersion/en?utm_source
 =artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Partially self-hosted\, partially at the 4DSOUND studio in Amsterd
 am\, and partially at KNMI in De Bilt near Utrecht\, Netherlands.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:futures-of-listening-worlding-narratives-roaming-sound-space-2027@artif
 icialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260916T111243Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260913
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260914
SUMMARY:Deadline: Futures of Listening: Worlding Narratives\, Roaming Sound
  Space Residency
DESCRIPTION:One residency to research and develop an interactive listening 
 experience built on non-linear sound narratives\, experienced by navigatin
 g through a series of virtual spaces or layers. NO VISUALS: Worlding Narra
 tives centres sound as the primary medium for immersion and intentionally 
 removes dominant visual layers such as VR\, AR\, projection or video. THE 
 DESIGN PROBLEM they want tackled is translation and adaptation\, specifica
 lly the shift from one visitor in a headphone-mediated experience to rende
 ring for a multi-speaker system for group interaction. That change in dyna
 mics\, reproduction and perspective is integral to the residency scope. RE
 SEARCH QUESTIONS include how immersive sound can function as a primary nar
 rative medium across speculative and non-fictional realities\, what new na
 rrative structures and dramaturgical methods become possible when the crea
 tive process originates from sound rather than adapting frameworks from ot
 her media\, and how interactive sonic structures can create navigable list
 ening experiences designed for and by multiple intelligences. Outcomes may
  include interactive sonic prototypes\, spatial audio compositions\, immer
 sive listening experiences\, narrative sound works or software prototypes.
  WORTH NOTING: your residency runs in tandem with resident Pinar Temiz\, a
 n expert in sound design for gaming environments\, with the opportunity to
  work together. Lead researcher is Dr Angela McArthur of UCL\, with resear
 ch support from Dr meLe yamomo of the University of Amsterdam. WHO: media 
 and sound artists\, sound designers\, musicians producing their own sonic 
 work\, field recordists\, writers\, composers and game sound designers. Ex
 perience with interactive audio\, spatial sound tools or game-sound workfl
 ows is welcome but not required. HARD ELIGIBILITY GATE: applicants must be
  based in the Netherlands AND registered as an artist with the Dutch Chamb
 er of Commerce (KvK). This is not negotiable and rules out non-NL applican
 ts. Futures of Listening is a Netherlands-based platform for spatial sound
 \, immersive experience\, performance and installation art\, founded by FI
 BER Festival\, 4DSOUND\, Robin Koek and Art of Sound at the Royal Conserva
 toire The Hague\, supported by CIIIC and Stimuleringsfonds.\n\nOrganisatio
 n: Futures of Listening (FIBER\, 4DSOUND\, Robin Koek\, Art of Sound)\nLoc
 ation: Amsterdam\, Netherlands\, with remote and studio access to the 4DSO
 UND infrastructure.\nAward: Total residency fee of EUR 7\,125\, calculated
  as 25 commissioned days at a day rate of EUR 285. Six of those 25 days ca
 n be spent at the 4DSOUND studio working with their team. Some additional 
 financial support is available if needed\, including material and travel c
 osts\, but these must be clearly defined and agreed before the residency s
 tarts. No application fee.\nDuration: January to March 2027\, structured a
 s 25 commissioned days\, running in tandem with fellow Worlding Narratives
  resident Pinar Temiz. Deadline 13 September 2026.\n\nMore: https://fiber.
 homerun.co/artist-residency-worlding-narratives/en?utm_source=artificialno
 uveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://fiber.homerun.co/artist-residency-worlding-narratives/en?utm_so
 urce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Amsterdam\, Netherlands\, with remote and studio access to the 4DS
 OUND infrastructure.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:making-space-guangzhou-nl-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260916T111243Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261003
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261004
SUMMARY:Deadline: Making Space Residency 2027 for Netherlands-Based Practit
 ioners (Guangzhou)
DESCRIPTION:The Embassy of the Kingdom of the Netherlands in China\, in par
 tnership with artist-run space Making Space in Guangzhou\, invites Netherl
 ands-based artists\, makers\, curators\, writers\, researchers and other c
 ultural practitioners to a six-week residency in spring 2027. Making Space
  (est. 2017) focuses on art and social practice with an emphasis on long-t
 erm research\, local knowledge and care-driven collaboration. The residenc
 y is process-oriented with no obligation to produce finished work\; the re
 sident takes part in at least one public exchange (talk\, workshop\, readi
 ng group\, screening\, performance or open studio). SUPPORT: EUR 2\,700 tr
 avel and artist fee subsidy (fixed per application\; duos or collectives s
 hare the amount)\, accommodation in Guangzhou\, shared studio space\, cura
 torial and research support with access to local networks\, and logistical
  support for public programming (extra funding may be considered for publi
 c programmes). The resident arranges their own China visa\; Making Space p
 rovides an invitation letter. LOOKING FOR: practitioners engaging with alt
 ernative education\, ecological justice\, migration and labour\, social pr
 actice\, intergenerational narratives\, diaspora and transdisciplinary col
 laboration\; English communication required. APPLY by email (makingspace20
 17@gmail.com) with a 200-word bio\, CV\, 2-page project proposal and portf
 olio (max 20 pages) in a single PDF\, in English. Result expected late Nov
 ember 2026. Deadline: 3 October 2026\, 23:59 CST / 17:59 CEST.\n\nOrganisa
 tion: Making Space\, in partnership with the Embassy of the Kingdom of the
  Netherlands in China\nLocation: Guangzhou\, China\nAward: EUR 2\,700 trav
 el and artist fee subsidy (fixed per application\; duos or collectives sha
 re it)\, plus accommodation in Guangzhou and shared studio space\nDuration
 : Six continuous weeks between 15 March and 15 June 2027\, dates agreed wi
 th the selected resident\n\nMore: https://makingspace2017.notion.site/open
 -call?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://makingspace2017.notion.site/open-call?utm_source=artificialnouv
 eaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Guangzhou\, China
END:VEVENT
